Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 18:06:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20automatic=20Claude=E2=86=92Codex=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?quota=20fallback=20per=20agent=20group?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the primary provider fails a turn with a quota-exhaustion error
(usage limit reached, hard rate limit, empty credit balance), the
unanswered prompt is retried once on the configured fallback provider
and the user is notified of the switch. Every new turn starts on the
primary again, so recovery is automatic — the first successful primary
turn after a fallback sends a 'back on Claude' notice.

- container_configs.fallback_provider column (migration 017), exposed
  via 'ncl groups config update --fallback-provider codex|none'
- host merges the fallback provider's mounts/env into the spawn args so
  its auth reaches the container alongside the primary's
- fallback keeps its own continuation slot, so the overflow
  conversation has memory across quota episodes
- claude provider now classifies quota correctly: is_error results
  matching the quota regex, and rate_limit_event only when rejected
  (previously any rate_limit_event was marked quota)
- off by default; no behavior change for groups without the flag

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
